==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{term|per||through|lang=la}} + {{term|sono|sonō|make a noise, sound, resound|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈper.so.noː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|persono|personō|personare|personāre|personui|personuī|personatum|personātum}}

# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I [[sound]] through and through, [[resound]], [[ring]].
# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I make a sound on a [[musical instrument]], [[play]], sound.
# {{transitive|lang=la}} I [[fill]] with sound, make resound.
# {{transitive|rare|lang=la}} I [[cry out]], [[call]] aloud.

====Inflection====
* Note that [[personavit|personāvit]] is an alternative form for the third-person singular perfect active indicative [[personuit]].
{{la-conj-1st|person|personu|personāt|33=personat}}

